{#- ============================================================================
    v6 "tl" — ports the mockup's #tl section (src6/v6-tl.html + src6/v6.js's
    MILES array) onto the site's existing journey content (c.journey), which
    the about page renders today via blocks.html.j2's sec_journey(). Same
    eyebrow/title/lead — the H2 in the mockup is word-for-word the existing
    c.journey.title, so nothing there was rewritten.

    The mockup builds this as a horizontal zigzag: a lime rail across the
    middle, one circular node per milestone, cards alternating above/below the
    rail on a CSS grid, each joined to the rail by a short vertical stem. All
    of that was built by v6.js at runtime (MILES.forEach + DOM writes) — this
    port renders the same grid statically in Jinja instead, alternating
    above/below with :nth-child(odd/even) so no JS is needed to decide which
    half a card belongs to.

    Content: c.journey (existing) supplies eyebrow/title/lead/items[].year,
    .title, .text — unchanged keys, since tools/build_site.py's JSON-LD
    milestone list reads c.journey.items[i].year/.title directly and an
    in-place edit to items[] risked breaking that. The new figures (the
    mockup's `ha` — running land-bank hectares per milestone, plus two
    labels) live in src6/content-tl.json under c.journey.count_label,
    c.journey.bank_label and a sibling list c.journey.milestone_ha (keyed by
    `year`, same key-based join v6/geo.html.j2 uses for its distance_meta),
    assumed merged into content/*.json by the build. Figures are the
    mockup's own MILES array, verbatim.

    The counter — "14 200 / ГЕКТАРІВ У БАНКУ" in the mockup's top-right — is
    driven there by an IntersectionObserver tweening 800 -> 14400 over 2.6s.
    No new JS is permitted, so it renders as a plain data-count element: the
    site's existing app.js already tweens any [data-count] into view (same
    hook the stats section uses) and prints the final formatted figure
    outright under reduced motion or without GSAP. The number is simply the
    last milestone's own ha value rather than an invented duplicate — one
    source for it, not two that could drift.

    Imported with context from blocks.html.j2, so `c`, `V` are already in
    scope, matching v6/geo.html.j2 and v6/why.html.j2.
    ============================================================================ -#}

{%- macro section() -%}
{%- set items = c.journey['items'] -%}
{#- year -> ha, joined by the shared `year` key rather than by position, so
    the two lists (items[] from content/*.json, milestone_ha[] from
    content-tl.json) cannot silently drift apart if either is reordered. -#}
{%- set ha_by_year = {} -%}
{%- for row in c.journey.milestone_ha %}{% set _ = ha_by_year.update({row.year: row.ha}) %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set total_ha = ha_by_year[items[-1].year] -%}
{#- Which milestones get the mockup's lime year-pill treatment (its MILES
    array's `key:1` flag) rather than the plain grey pill — indices 0, 4, 5
    of six (2008, 2022, 2026), not simply "first and last". -#}
{%- set key_idx = [0, items|length - 2, items|length - 1] -%}
<section class="section jtl" id="journey" role="region" aria-labelledby="jr-t">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head-row jtl__head">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="tag tag--lime" data-r>{{ c.journey.eyebrow }}</span>
        <h2 id="jr-t" data-split>{{ c.journey.title }}</h2>
        <p class="lead" data-r>{{ c.journey.lead }}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="jtl__count" data-r="right">
        {#- Bigger figures count for longer — same rule stat_card() uses. -#}
        <b class="jtl__count-n" data-count="{{ total_ha }}" data-dur="2.4">0</b>
        <span>{{ c.journey.count_label }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="jtl__grid">
      <div class="jtl__rail" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div>

      <ol class="jtl__list" data-stagger=".08">
        {%- for m in items %}
        <li class="jtl__item">
          <span class="jtl__node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <article class="jtl__card{{ ' jtl__card--key' if loop.index0 in key_idx }}">
            <span class="jtl__yr">{{ m.year }}</span>
            <h3 class="jtl__t">{{ m.title }}</h3>
            <p class="jtl__d">{{ m.text }}</p>
            <div class="jtl__ha">
              <span>{{ c.journey.bank_label }}</span>
              <b>{{ fmt_num(ha_by_year[m.year]) }}&nbsp;{{ ha }}</b>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}
